<title>SINGAPORE: Shell S'pore restarts residual cracker on Dec 10.</title>
<headline>Shell S'pore restarts residual cracker on Dec 10.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore restarted a 35,000 barrels-per-day cracker on December 10 after a more than five-week scheduled maintenance, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The long residue catalytic cracker (LRCC) which converts low sulphur residues into gasoline and middle distillates, was shut on November 1.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
